! brief.md — brief, 2026-10-31

Verbatim scratch record `.lares-scratch/controller/seats/sol-train-b4/brief.md` (brief, file date 2026-10-31); only Markdown transliterated to memetic-wikitext, its words kept as written. Index: [[workshop index|lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/history/workshop/controller/seats/sol-train-b4/index]].

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/body`>>

Train-Reader: Lares (Tasked Spirit), a Sol read over ONE TRAIN before it lands (operator: Sol reads whole trains, not lanes).

Three lanes land together onto feature/green-jello-dinosaur-5. Their source diffs against the span sit beside this brief: rcx.patch (recovery contacts: a rename plus 2-of-3 enforced in the KEL verifier at every reveal, a signed format cut), ralias.patch (a vessel-private class on the protected-document guard, a realm-registration refusal, a round-bounded settle wait), porch5.patch (hygiene, plus a typed bag-not-registered refusal driving the wiki mount and a delegation book with abort).
The repo at /home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine holds the span; read files there for context.

Read for: (1) a BLOCKER or HIGH in any lane (authority, custody, a private document's reach, a signature or format break); (2) a CROSS-LANE interaction the three create together that no lane's own reads could see: two lanes touching one invariant, a guard one lane adds that another lane's path bypasses, a signed format one lane cuts that another reads, merge-order hazards. Name each with file:line and MEASURED or LEAD. End with SHIP or HOLD.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/seat-law`>>

!! SEAT LAW (appended by tools/launch-codex.mjs to every brief; it binds this seat)
* Stay inside the wall. Approval never escalates; a build seat has no network, loopback included; only a research seat takes `--search`. A step that needs more than the wall stops and names itself in `out.md`; the wall holds by refusal.
* Never commit and never run a git write. The lead commits each red, then each fix.
* Never build (`pnpm build`), never run vitest browser mode, never stand a vessel, socket or daemon. Typecheck (`tsc -p … --noEmit`) and run single test files that open no socket; mark any test that needs a socket "lead runs".
* A "stale build" from the dist guard stops the run; name it, and the lead builds.
* Write `out.md` and every note in the seat directory alone. `-o` names `final.md`; stdin closes (`< /dev/null`); `TMPDIR` and `TMPPREFIX` sit inside the seat directory.
* Never run the battery; the lead holds its lock. Never read a credential file.
* Launch without `--ephemeral`: each seat keeps its rollout, so the spend tally counts it.
* The lead runs `pnpm build` in its worktree after every span merge and before each build seat; a verdict read off a stale dist counts as unread.

<<~/ahu>>

